    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "snqfaoe",
      "content": "The Bhilai Steel Plant (BSP) is India's first integrated steel plant set up with the cooperation of the erstwhile Soviet Union (Russia). It was established in 1955 and production started in 1959. BSP is located in Bhilai in the Durg district. It is operated by Steel Authority of India Limited (SAIL) and is one of the largest integrated steel plants in Asia."
    },
